1
00:00:00,160 --> 00:00:06,320
Hello everyone, this is Frank Di Freitas and welcome to a special broadcast of HoloTalk.

2
00:00:14,240 --> 00:00:23,840
So I would like to take this opportunity to thank you for inviting me and Mario Andres into your homes, your schools, and your businesses.

3
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:42,000
We're going to do this broadcast so that you can learn a little bit about lasers and holography.

4
00:01:47,720 --> 00:01:58,040
Holograms can appear so real that sometimes you are fooled into thinking that what you are seeing is right in front of you.

5
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:07,800
You may wish to reach out and try and touch the image in a hologram.

6
00:02:12,040 --> 00:02:14,760
But your hand just passes right through.

7
00:02:53,960 --> 00:02:56,840
And advertising comerciales.

8
00:02:56,840 --> 00:03:01,240
You may buy a box of cereal and see a hologram on the box.

9
00:03:18,360 --> 00:03:22,920
If you wear jeans, you may find holograms on your clothes.

10
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:31,320
So that they are not counterfeited.

11
00:03:34,840 --> 00:03:38,200
And in museums you may see holograms as fine art.

12
00:03:41,760 --> 00:03:47,280
Where artists use the three-dimensional properties of holography to express themselves.

13
00:03:55,680 --> 00:04:04,240
Now at this point you may be asking what do holograms and lasers have in common.

14
00:04:06,800 --> 00:04:13,120
Well the truth is you do not need a laser to see a hologram, but you need a laser to make one.

15
00:05:24,400 --> 00:05:28,320
And some day you may find yourself working with lasers as your job.

16
00:05:33,480 --> 00:05:36,680
With holography, we use lasers to make holograms.

17
00:05:40,760 --> 00:05:45,560
A laser provides the special light needed in order to make the hologram.

18
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:59,560
There are gas lasers.

19
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:12,120
When electricity is applied to the gas in the tube, it begins to glow.

20
00:06:18,920 --> 00:06:25,160
And it is reflected back and forth between two mirrors that are on the ends of the tube.

21
00:06:33,720 --> 00:06:37,400
And exits through one of the mirrors as a laser beam.

22
00:07:08,800 --> 00:07:11,680
Which is made specially for holograms.

23
00:07:15,760 --> 00:07:19,360
Recently we found a new way to make holograms.

24
00:07:23,280 --> 00:07:27,520
And we do not require the very expensive gas lasers.

25
00:07:33,040 --> 00:07:38,400
We use very inexpensive lasers called laser diodes.

26
00:07:57,120 --> 00:08:00,640
And we have made holograms using a laser pointer.

27
00:08:14,240 --> 00:08:17,760
Because it opens the field up to very, very many people.

28
00:08:46,840 --> 00:08:50,440
I know we didn't have a lot of time to cover very many things.

29
00:08:55,240 --> 00:09:00,760
But I hope it at least make you a little more interested in lasers and holography.

30
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:09,480
And on your own, you will search out information on the field.

31
00:09:14,440 --> 00:09:20,040
So I would like to thank Mario Andres Muniz for doing the translations for this show.

32
00:09:54,440 --> 00:09:55,080
Good day.
